--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@ Small command-line tool the ops team uses to summarise event logs exported from
 
 prints one line per service and level with the number of events, then a total.
 
+To look at recent events only, add `--since`:
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+This counts events at or after that moment. A plain date means 00:00 UTC on that day; a full ISO datetime (e.g. `2024-03-10T12:00:00+02:00`) is also accepted, and one without an offset is UTC. Events are compared in UTC, whatever offset they were stamped with. An invalid value gives an error message and exit status 2.
+
 Each line of an events file is a JSON object:
 
     {"ts": "2024-03-09T23:30:00-05:00", "service": "api", "level": "error", "msg": "upstream timeout"}
